{
  "$comment": [
    "The one place colour is decided. `pnpm run theme` turns this into",
    "src/themeTokens.generated.ts, which the app reads at startup and on",
    "every theme switch — both for the CSS custom properties and for the",
    "colours handed to the wasm renderer.",
    "",
    "Everything is authored in OKLCH. In that space lightness and chroma",
    "mean the same thing at every hue, so a set of colours written with",
    "one lightness and one chroma reads as one family. Written in hex,",
    "the same set drifts: the palette this replaced ran from L 0.56 to",
    "L 0.94 and from C 0.11 to C 0.30, which is why some colours shouted",
    "and others disappeared.",
    "",
    "Chroma is deliberately low. C 0.12 is about two thirds of what the",
    "old palette used, and at that strength eight hues can sit next to",
    "each other without any of them taking over."
  ],

  "hues": {
    "red": 25,
    "orange": 62,
    "yellow": 98,
    "green": 152,
    "teal": 192,
    "blue": 255,
    "purple": 300,
    "pink": 342
  },

  "$comment_lift": [
    "Perceptual uniformity is the starting point, not the finish. A",
    "yellow at the same lightness as a blue looks muddy — yellow only",
    "reads as yellow when it is light. Each hue gets a lift, applied to",
    "every step, which is the tuning a flat ramp needs."
  ],
  "lift": {
    "red": 0.0,
    "orange": 0.04,
    "yellow": 0.1,
    "green": 0.02,
    "teal": 0.02,
    "blue": -0.02,
    "purple": -0.02,
    "pink": 0.0
  },

  "steps": {
    "dim": { "lightness": 0.5, "chroma": 0.085 },
    "base": { "lightness": 0.7, "chroma": 0.12 },
    "bright": { "lightness": 0.84, "chroma": 0.115 }
  },

  "$comment_neutral": [
    "Neutrals carry a trace of blue (C 0.006 at hue 255). Dead grey on a",
    "dark screen reads slightly warm against the coloured labels; this",
    "is small enough that nobody calls it blue and large enough that the",
    "greys stop fighting the hues.",
    "",
    "Step numbers are lightness in percent, so 8 is L 0.08. They stay",
    "the same across themes: a light theme reverses which end the",
    "surfaces come from, not what the numbers mean."
  ],
  "neutral": {
    "hue": 255,
    "chroma": 0.006,
    "steps": [4, 8, 11, 14, 18, 24, 32, 42, 52, 62, 72, 82, 92, 97]
  },

